<title>USA: Clinton sees &quot;encouraging&quot; budget talks.</title>
<headline>Clinton sees &quot;encouraging&quot; budget talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton on Friday said &quot;encouraging&quot; progress had been made in budget talks with the Republican-controlled Congress but acknowledged that serious differences remained.</p>
<p>&quot;The progress we've made so far is encouraging,&quot; Clinton said during a brief news conference at the White House. He stressed, however, that tough negotiations remained.  </p>
<p>&quot;I don't believe that an agreement at any price is worth doing,&quot; Clinton said.</p>
<p>He said that next week was not necessarily &quot;make or break&quot; for the talks, despite claims a deadline was nearing.</p>
</text>
